            <ArticleTitle>[A man with a painful hand after punching a wall].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A9495</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 23-year-old man had a painful right hand after punching a wall. The base of the second metacarpal was swollen and painful. The base of the second metacarpal is difficult to assess radiologically, due to overlying structures. After a trauma, additional slight oblique X-rays may help to make a diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
